---
// Refund Policy — "Page: Refund Policy" (#41), PM-authored, verbatim. MoR wording is
// GENERIC per PM's 2026-06-11 decision (no provider named until #31 approval); the
// named form is the on-approval target in site-copy-twiceover.md. Do not reword (PM #41).
import Policy from "../layouts/Policy.astro";
import { EMAIL } from "../config.mjs";
---
<Policy
  title="Refund Policy — TwiceOver"
  description="Refund Policy for TwiceOver — twiceover.io."
  heading="Refunds"
>
  <p>TwiceOver is sold as a subscription, billed by a third-party merchant of record.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cancel anytime.</strong> Cancelling stops future renewals; you keep access through the end of the paid period.</li>
    <li><strong>Refund requests.</strong> To request a refund, contact <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> or use the merchant-of-record's billing portal. Eligible refunds are processed by our merchant of record under their buyer terms.</li>
    <li><strong>Where required by law,</strong> statutory cancellation and refund rights (for example, EU/UK consumer cooling-off rights) apply and are honored.</li>
    <li>No per-analysis or usage charges exist, so there is nothing to refund beyond the subscription itself.</li>
  </ul>
</Policy>
